    <!-- ================================================================================
         Smart Servos (AP) — FASTER VIKING TRANSFORM half of the WoLUUpgSmartServos passive
         face (the attack-while-moving half is a per-player Weapon.AllowedMovement=Moving edit
         in genlib.py). Morph durations live in nested indexed-array fields
         (Abil,<morph>,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[*].DurationArray[*]) → a per-player runtime
         CatalogFieldValueModify on them is a NOOP (the indexed-array no-op class). The
         rule-9-safe lever is a player-only CUpgrade EffectArray (Operation="Subtract"), the
         VERIFIED rogue Kit@AISmartServos pattern (mods/_reference/rogue/GameData/UpgradeData.xml
         CUpgrade Kit@AISmartServos). Granted ONLY to the human player by our library
         (libWoLU_GrantCampaignTech, next to the WoLUnbalancedFlag grant), so this global static
         EffectArray edit is effectively player-only → rule-9-safe (same class as
         CombatShield/RegenerativeBioSteel above).

         COVERAGE (rules 4/10): the base Viking (AssaultMode/FighterMode) AND the Hel's Angels
         merc — which use SEPARATE morph ability ids WreckingCrewAssaultMode/WreckingCrewFighterMode
         (standalone, inherit NOTHING from the base Viking morphs), so they need their OWN
         EffectArray entries.

         VALUES verified against the ACTUAL morph defs (cited durations from the reference dump),
         each cut to leave the gameplay-relevant Stats.Duration (form-switch instant) + the
         cosmetic Actor.Duration at ~1.0 s, and the Mover physics fields ≥ 0.2 s (never to 0 or
         negative):
           Base AssaultMode  (liberty.sc2mod/AbilData.xml:1410): Actor.Duration=2.34,
             Mover.Delay=0.533, Mover.Duration=1.2, Stats.Duration=2.34 (no Collide section).
           Base FighterMode  (liberty.sc2mod/AbilData.xml:1431): Actor.Duration=2.333,
             Collide.Delay=1.5, Mover.Delay=0.6, Mover.Duration=0.85, Stats.Duration=2.333.
           HelsAngels WreckingCrewAssaultMode (liberty.sc2campaign/AbilData.xml:2991):
             Actor.Duration=2.334, Mover.Delay=0.9333, Mover.Duration=1.4, Stats.Duration=2.333.
           HelsAngels WreckingCrewFighterMode (liberty.sc2campaign/AbilData.xml:3014):
             Actor.Duration=2.333, Collide.Delay=1.5, Mover.Delay=0.666, Mover.Duration=1.667,
             Stats.Duration=2.333.
         (We cut only the Stats/Actor + the two base Mover fields the rogue kit cuts; we do NOT
         touch Collide.Delay — leaving it preserves a clean physics transition. The Hel's Angels
         entries cut only Stats+Actor → form-switch ~1.0 s, same proportion as the base Viking.) -->
    <CUpgrade id="WoLUSmartServos">
        <EditorCategories value="Race:Terran"/>
        <!-- Base Viking → Assault (ground) mode -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,AssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Actor].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.340000"/>   <!-- 2.34 -> 1.0 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,AssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Mover].DurationArray[Delay]" Value="0.333000"/>      <!-- 0.533 -> 0.2 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,AssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Mover].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="0.200000"/>   <!-- 1.2 -> 1.0 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,AssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Stats].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.340000"/>   <!-- 2.34 -> 1.0 (form-switch) -->
        <!-- Base Viking → Fighter (air) mode -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,FighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Actor].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>   <!-- 2.333 -> 1.0 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,FighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Mover].DurationArray[Delay]" Value="0.300000"/>      <!-- 0.6 -> 0.3 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,FighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Mover].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="0.150000"/>   <!-- 0.85 -> 0.7 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,FighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Stats].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>   <!-- 2.333 -> 1.0 (form-switch) -->
        <!-- Hel's Angels (Viking merc) → Assault mode (separate morph id) -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,WreckingCrewAssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Actor].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>  <!-- 2.334 -> 1.001 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,WreckingCrewAssaultMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Stats].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>  <!-- 2.333 -> 1.0 -->
        <!-- Hel's Angels (Viking merc) → Fighter mode (separate morph id) -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,WreckingCrewFighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Actor].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>  <!-- 2.333 -> 1.0 -->
        <EffectArray Operation="Subtract" Reference="Abil,WreckingCrewFighterMode,InfoArray[0].SectionArray[Stats].DurationArray[Duration]" Value="1.333000"/>  <!-- 2.333 -> 1.0 -->
    </CUpgrade>

    <!-- ================================================================================
         ITEM 1b (v0.3.30): NEUTRALIZE the wrapper ROOT upgrades (FAMILY D).
         libWoLU_DisableArmoryResearch still GRANTS the wrapper LevelN
         (Terran{Vehicle,Ship}{Weapons,Armors}{UltraCapacitors,VanadiumPlating}LevelN)
         to the human player so the libertystory Armory buttons (Research16-27)
         auto-hide (a CAbilResearch button hides once its target upgrade is
         QueuedOrBetter). Those wrapper LevelN are icon-only in their OWN body BUT
         INHERIT the wrapper ROOT stat via parent= (so granting them was silently
         adding a SECOND +3 (weapon/armor levels, +5% HP) on every listed unit on top
         of family A). We zero the ROOT stat here so the still-granted wrapper LevelN
         contributes 0 levels: buttons stay hidden, no double-apply. Full-restate-with-
         explicit-indices (the RegenerativeBioSteel pattern) so no duplicate/fighting
         entries exist; every real stat (Weapon Level / Effect Amount / AttributeBonus /
         LifeArmor / LifeArmorLevel / RateMultiplier) -> 0, every Operation="Multiply"
         LifeMax/LifeStart (x1.05 HP) -> 1 (no-op multiply). These ROOTs have NO icon Set
         entries (icons live in the LevelN bodies, not the ROOT), so nothing display-only
         is touched. RULE 9: WoL never grants these wrapper ROOTs (or the wrapper LevelN)
         to enemies (only our per-player libWoLU_DisableArmoryResearch grants the LevelN
         to the human), so this global static edit is effectively player-only; enemy
         vehicles/ships are untouched.

         v0.3.31 UPDATE — the ROOT-zero override below did NOT neutralize the inherited
         stat in game (owner still saw 6/6), because the campaign defines these 4 wrapper
         ROOTs default="1" (ref UpgradeData.xml:221/318/394/467) and our non-default same-id
         ROOT-zero override did not replace the template. The PRIMARY neutralizer is now the
         parent re-point of the 12 wrapper LevelN to the BODYLESS Talent super-roots
         UltraCapacitors / VanadiumPlating (see the block after these ROOTs) — with a bodyless
         parent the LevelN inherits ZERO stat regardless of the ROOT state. The ROOT-zero
         overrides below (now carrying default="1" to match the campaign template) are kept
         as belt-and-suspenders safety nets. -->

