    <!-- ================================================================================
         ITEM 1b PRIMARY NEUTRALIZER (v0.3.31): RE-POINT the 12 wrapper LevelN parents to
         the BODYLESS Talent super-roots. The wrapper LevelN
         (Terran{Vehicle,Ship}{Weapons,Armors}{UltraCapacitors,VanadiumPlating}Level{1,2,3})
         are still GRANTED to the human by libWoLU_DisableArmoryResearch ONLY so the
         libertystory Armory buttons auto-hide. In their OWN body each LevelN carries just
         <Icon>, <ScoreAmount>, and icon Set EffectArrays — the real +1/level STAT is
         INHERITED from its stat-bearing wrapper ROOT via parent=. The v0.3.30 ROOT-zero
         overrides did NOT neutralize that inherited stat in game (the campaign ROOTs are
         default="1" — ref UpgradeData.xml:221/318/394/467 — so our non-default same-id
         override did not replace the template; owner still read 6/6).

         FIX: re-point each LevelN's parent= to the BODYLESS Talent super-root
         (UltraCapacitors for weapons, VanadiumPlating for armor — ref UpgradeData.xml:670/674:
         only <EditorCategories> + the UpgradeCheat flag, NO EffectArray, NO parent ⇒ inherits
         ZERO stat). These are parent-ONLY self-closing same-id overrides: setting just the
         parent= attribute changes the parent while the LevelN's OWN body (its icon Set
         entries) is preserved by field-merge (re-parenting is reference-keyed, not positional)
         — so the icon Sets are NOT orphaned, the Armory button still hides on grant, and icons
         still show. With the parent now bodyless the LevelN adds 0 levels/armor/HP, regardless
         of the ROOT state. This is the PRIMARY neutralizer; the ROOT-zero overrides above +
         their default="1" are belt-and-suspenders safety nets.

         RULE 9: same player-only-in-effect basis as the ROOT-zero block above — WoL grants
         these wrapper LevelN only to the human (libWoLU_DisableArmoryResearch); enemies never
         get them, so this global static re-parent is effectively player-only. Family A (base
         Terran{Vehicle,Ship}{Weapons,Armors}LevelN) remains the SINGLE +3 scaling source. -->

